**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `unit-tests`: `BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests`, `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`

**How to implement.** The transparent triclinic ground truth moves into `BerremanTestSupport` whole (001 §Q AT-2 'The ground truth and designs (`BiaxialSample.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs`: constants, …) move into a shared test-support project'; 001 §S10 'holding `BiaxialSample` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample`'; the S10.2 brief). This is a MOVE (.spec-md §4 'A reuse is a move or a call: the new home is created and the old body deleted in the same step'; .spec-md §7 'Harness and samples (test → product / test support) … Migration provided: a move'): after the step exactly one `BiaxialSample` module exists. (1) `git mv Berreman/BerremanTests/BiaxialSample.fs Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs`, and its namespace becomes `BerremanTestSupport`. Every declaration moves with its body unchanged, as S10.1 leaves it: `referenceWaveLength`, the three indices and the six gyration components, `triclinic`, `solverParameters`, `scalingAround`, `opticAxisFromLargest`, `opticAxisWaveNormal`, `epsDiagonal`, `rhoImaginary` and `recoveredQuantities`. The retained `BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic` MUST move with the module and MUST call `TriclinicParameters.opticalProperties`, whose tensor kernel was extracted in step 333, and `recoveredQuantities` has named `ParameterName`s and read `QuantityValue`s since step 341. Its opens are unchanged. It reads no name of the `BerremanTests` namespace, and `BerremanTestSupport` references no test project. In the module doc, only what the move makes untrue changes. The first sentence's 'every biaxial suite in this assembly shares' (`BiaxialSample.fs:13`) becomes 'every biaxial suite shares', and that paragraph gains one sentence citing spec 0050 S10.2 (001 §Q AT-2): the sample lives in `BerremanTestSupport`, so one compiled copy serves `BerremanTests` and `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`. In the spec R3 sentence, 'in the TEST assembly' (`BiaxialSample.fs:23`) becomes 'in test code'. Every other doc line keeps its text. (2) `BerremanTestSupport.fsproj` gains `<Compile Include="BiaxialSample.fs" />` after `CommittedKits.fs`. It also gains the project reference to `..\OpticalConstructor\OpticalConstructor.Optimization\OpticalConstructor.Optimization.fsproj` after the Domain one, because `RecoveredQuantity` and `QuantityValue` are `OpticalConstructor.Optimization`'s (steps 341 and 338). No comment is added. (3) `BerremanTests.fsproj` deletes `<Compile Include="BiaxialSample.fs" />` with the comment above it (`BerremanTests.fsproj:40-41`). It also deletes the comment above `<Compile Include="InverseFitHarness.fs" />` (`BerremanTests.fsproj:36-38`), which S10.1 made untrue: after step 343 the harness declares no type and drives no fit. The `InverseFitHarness.fs` line keeps its place. (4) The consumers read the moved module. `open BerremanTests.BiaxialSample` becomes `open BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`, keeping its trailing comment, in `BiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialInverseTests.fs`, `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests.fs` and `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fs` (which step 346 moves). Nothing else in them changes. BerremanTests' numbers are bit-identical (.spec-md §4 'BerremanTests' numbers stay unchanged'; 001 §S10 '`BerremanTests` stays green with unchanged numbers'): every expression is unchanged, and only its namespace moves. No test is added or removed. `FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests` (about 104 s) drives `triclinic`, `scalingAround`, `opticAxisWaveNormal`, `solverParameters` and `referenceWaveLength`. `BiaxialInverseTests` (about 997 s) is selected too, because it alone reaches `epsDiagonal`, `rhoImaginary`, `opticAxisFromLargest` and `recoveredQuantities`; the S10.2 brief names both classes. The moved test-support module MUST still declare buildTriclinic; every direct test caller MUST use the new namespace, and the old BerremanTests source MUST be deleted. Product code MUST use the parameter-record member and MUST NOT reference BerremanTestSupport. This preserves 001 §Q's named builder destination without copying physics.

**Acceptance.** After the move, `Berreman/BerremanTestSupport/BiaxialSample.fs` MUST declare the module `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample` with every declaration and number unchanged. `Berreman/BerremanTests/` MUST neither hold nor compile `BiaxialSample.fs`, and every consumer MUST open `BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample`. unit-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, `BerremanTests.BiaxialInverseTests` and `BerremanTests.FeasibleBiaxialInverseTests`, their numbers and counts unchanged; and build, elevation and the twenty s34 invariants MUST pass. BerremanTestSupport.BiaxialSample.buildTriclinic MUST exist and call the shared product kernel; the former BerremanTests source MUST be absent.
